---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import DocNav from '../components/DocNav.astro';
import '../styles/global.css';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — Prabal Banerjee"
  description="About Prabal Banerjee: Co-Founder of Avail, previously Lead Researcher at Polygon, and a cryptography researcher from the Indian Statistical Institute, Kolkata."
>
  <div class="terminal-content">
    <DocNav current="about" />

    <main>
      <section id="about" class="doc">
        <h1 class="sr-only">About Prabal Banerjee</h1>
        <div class="terminal-prompt-line" aria-hidden="true">$ cat about.txt</div>

        <p>
          I am Prabal Banerjee, co-founder of <a href="https://www.availproject.org/">Avail</a>, where
          I lead research and engineering. Avail is a modular blockchain infrastructure project built
          around data availability — the problem of making sure that the data behind a block has
          actually been published, so that anybody who wants to verify a chain is able to.
        </p>

        <p>
          Before Avail I was Lead Researcher at Polygon (previously Matic Network) from 2020 to 2023,
          working on improving a production proof-of-stake chain, contributing to scaling work such as
          zkRollups, and designing, prototyping and leading the development of Avail itself while it
          was still inside Polygon.
        </p>

        <p>
          My academic background is in cryptology. I was a PhD student at the Cryptology and Security
          Research Unit of the Indian Statistical Institute, Kolkata, from 2016 to 2020, and left
          before finishing to work on blockchains full time. Before that I read for an MSc in Computer
          Science at the Chennai Mathematical Institute and a BSc (Hons) in Computer Science at St.
          Xavier's College, Kolkata. Along the way I interned with the blockchain teams at IBM
          Research India, with Xoken Labs, with Oracle, and at Jadavpur University.
        </p>

        <p>
          My published work sits mostly at the intersection of blockchains and cryptographic
          fairness: fair digital exchange, griefing attacks on the Lightning Network, decentralised
          marketplaces for content sharing, privacy-preserving data audit in the cloud, and
          proof-of-work schemes that do something useful. The full list, with links to the papers and
          their arXiv preprints, is on the <a href="/#publications">home page</a>.
        </p>

        <p>
          I write occasionally. Essays are listed under <a href="/#writings">writings</a>. The best
          way to reach me is on <a href="https://x.com/prabalbanerjee">X</a>; my code is on <a
          href="https://github.com/prabal-banerjee">GitHub</a> and my other contact details are on
          the <a href="/#contact">home page</a>.
        </p>

        <p class="back"><a href="/">&larr; back to the terminal</a></p>
      </section>
    </main>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .doc {
    max-width: 900px;
  }

  .doc p {
    color: var(--subtext);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    margin-bottom: 1.2rem;
    max-width: 72ch;
  }

  .doc .back {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
  }
</style>
